| Troy Goode | 144 (67.3%) | 159 (66.8%) | active, last commit 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 (9.3%) | 22 (9.2%) | inactive, last commit at this path 2017-10-04, anywhere 2021-09-07 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 14 (6.5%) | 16 (6.7%) | inactive, last commit 2015-05-28 |

- **Troy Goode's figure is a merge of two addresses.** It counts `<email redacted>` (132 lines, 61.7%, 147 counting blank lines) and `troy@laptop.example` (12 lines, 5.6%, 12 counting blank lines) as one person. That is a guess from the name and addresses, and you should confirm it. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` still tops the table at 61.7%.
- **If you want a second reviewer, Douglas Christopher Wilson is next by lines.** He has no commit in the past year, so he may be slow to respond. Troy Goode is the only active person with a real share. The other 19 authors hold small shares each.
- **Bus factor is 1 for this file.** That means Troy Goode alone holds over 50% of the lines (67.3% non-blank, 66.8% counting blank lines). It takes 3 authors to reach 80%. This counts concentration of lines, not who understands the code.
- **A reformat commit was set aside.** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes") rewrote 1,016 lines in 4 files, formatting only. Without that correction Troy Goode would hold 123 lines (57.5%), merged, so he still leads.
- **One more commit looks mechanical but was not set aside.** It is `fcd2b56`, "switch to ESLint; clean up", by Troy Goode, with 5 surviving lines. I did not inspect it.
- **Some lines are credited to the author, not the committer.** 11 lines of `e64e854` belong to Alejandro Caravaca Puchades, committed by Troy Goode. 6 lines of `f038e77` belong to LuisEGR, committed by Douglas Christopher Wilson.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades appears under two names.** The same address shows up as `alex94puchades`, and the 14 lines count them as one.

This counts who wrote the lines your change will touch, not who understands them. Since you haven't made the change yet, the real overlap may differ. Once you have a diff, `--for-diff main...<branch>` will name the authors of the lines it replaces.

